# Tauri 2's dev-mode file watcher uses this file (gitignore-syntax) to
# decide what to ignore inside src-tauri/. Without it, sing-box's
# runtime artefacts (rule-set cache, downloaded UI bundle, latency
# history) trigger a rebuild loop:
#
#   "File src-tauri\cache.db changed. Rebuilding application..."
#
# fires every few seconds while the proxy is up.

# sing-box rule-set cache + URL-test latency history. Written to CWD
# whenever sing-box runs; on Windows dev this lands in src-tauri/.
cache.db
cache.db-journal

# External clash dashboard sing-box auto-downloads when experimental.clash_api
# .external_ui is set. Same anchor reasoning as the gitignore rule.
ui/

# Runtime config + .bak files our own app writes via atomic_write —
# these aren't in src-tauri/ usually, but be defensive.
*.bak
*.bak.1
*.bak.2
*.bak.3

# Build/CI artefacts the cargo watch already covers — but listing them
# here is harmless and keeps the watcher quiet.
target/
gen/
